# Tailwind CSS Usage Rules for Next.js + Modus

## 🎯 Overview

This document outlines the proper usage of Tailwind CSS in Next.js applications with Modus Design System. The goal is to **maximize Tailwind utility classes** and **eliminate custom CSS classes** for better maintainability, consistency, and scalability.

**Key Principle**: Use Tailwind's built-in utilities (including `hover:`, `focus:`, `bg-*`, `text-*`, `style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }}*`) inline instead of creating custom CSS classes. This keeps your codebase lean and prevents `globals.css` from growing unmanageably.

## 🚫 NEVER Create Custom CSS Classes

**❌ DO NOT create custom CSS classes for styling:**

```css
/* ❌ NEVER DO THIS - Don't create custom classes */
.app-header {
  ...;
}
.nav-link {
  ...;
}
.card-bordered {
  ...;
}
.custom-button {
  ...;
}
```

**✅ ALWAYS use Tailwind inline:**

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Pure Tailwind
<div className="bg-background style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }} text-foreground">
<Link className="hover:bg-card">
<div className="bg-card border style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }} rounded-lg">
<ModusWcButton color="primary">
```

## 🎨 Core Principles

### ✅ ALWAYS Use Tailwind Classes Inline (Preferred)

**Best Approach - Pure Tailwind with Design System Colors:**

```tsx
// ✅ BEST - Pure Tailwind with design system colors
<div className="flex items-center justify-between p-4 rounded-lg bg-background style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }} text-foreground">
  Content
</div>

// ✅ BEST - Hover states inline with Tailwind
<Link
  href="/page"
  className="px-4 py-2 rounded transition-colors duration-200 text-foreground hover:bg-card no-underline"
>
  Link
</Link>

// ✅ BEST - Header/Footer with design system colors
<div className="w-full bg-background style={{ borderBottom: "1px solid var(--border)" }} text-foreground">
  <div className="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-4">Navigation</div>
</div>

<div className="text-center py-4 bg-card style={{ borderTop: "2px solid var(--border)" }} text-foreground">
  <div className="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4">Footer content</div>
</div>
```

### Why This Approach?

1. **✅ No Custom CSS Bloat**: Tailwind purges unused classes automatically
2. **✅ Self-Documenting**: All styling visible in the component
3. **✅ Better DX**: No jumping between files to understand styles
4. **✅ Scalable**: Won't grow unmanageably like custom CSS
5. **✅ Maintainable**: Easy to modify inline
6. **✅ Design System Integration**: Works perfectly with Modus colors

### ❌ NEVER Create Custom CSS Classes for Styling

**Only create custom CSS for these 2 cases:**

1. **Theme-based logo/icon switching** (can't be done with Tailwind)
2. **Complex animations** requiring `@keyframes`

**That's it. Everything else uses Tailwind inline.**

```css
/* ❌ NEVER DO THIS - Don't create custom classes */
.custom-header {
  background-color: var(--background);
  border-color: var(--border);
  color: var(--foreground);
}

.card-bordered {
  background-color: var(--card);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.nav-link:hover {
  background-color: var(--card);
}

/* ✅ INSTEAD - Use Tailwind inline */
<div className="bg-background style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }} text-foreground">
<div className="bg-card style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }}">
<Link className="hover:bg-card">
```

## 🎨 Modus Design System Color Integration

### ✅ Use Tailwind Classes with Design System Colors

Tailwind v4's `@theme inline` automatically makes our design system colors available as Tailwind classes:

```tsx
// ✅ Background colors
<div className="bg-background">Page background</div>
<div className="bg-card">Card background</div>
<div className="bg-muted">Muted background</div>
<div className="bg-primary">Primary background</div>

// ✅ Text colors
<div className="text-foreground">Main text</div>
<div className="text-muted-foreground">Subtle text</div>
<div className="text-primary">Primary text</div>
<div className="text-destructive">Error text</div>

// ✅ Border colors (use inline styles for borders)
<div style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }}>Standard border</div>
<div style={{ border: "1px solid var(--input)" }}>Input border</div>
<div className="focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring">Focus ring</div>

// ✅ Hover states
<ModusWcButton color="primary">
  Hover effect
</ModusWcButton>
<Link className="text-foreground hover:bg-card">
  Link with hover
</Link>
```

### Available Design System Colors

```tsx
// Background colors
bg - background, bg - foreground, bg - card, bg - popover;
bg - primary, bg - secondary, bg - muted, bg - accent;
bg - destructive, bg - border, bg - input, bg - ring;

// Text colors
text - background, text - foreground, text - card - foreground;
text - primary, text - primary - foreground;
text - secondary, text - secondary - foreground;
text - muted, text - muted - foreground;
text - accent, text - accent - foreground;
text - destructive, text - destructive - foreground;

// Border colors
border - border, border - input, border - ring;
```

### ❌ NEVER Use Original Modus CSS Variables Directly

```tsx
// ❌ Wrong - Don't use raw Modus variables
<div style={{ backgroundColor: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-page)" }}>

// ✅ Correct - Use design system colors
<div className="bg-background">
```

