## 🚫 Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### ❌ Don't Create Custom CSS for Simple Patterns

```css
/* ❌ WRONG - Unnecessary custom CSS */
.app-header {
  background-color: var(--background);
  border-color: var(--border);
  color: var(--foreground);
}

.nav-link:hover {
  background-color: var(--card);
}

.text-foreground {
  color: var(--foreground);
}
```

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Use Tailwind inline instead
<div className="bg-background text-foreground style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }}">
<Link className="hover:bg-card">
<div className="text-foreground">
```

### ❌ Don't Use Event Handlers for Hover States

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - JavaScript for hover states
<Link
  onMouseEnter={(e) => {
    e.currentTarget.style.backgroundColor = "var(--card)";
  }}
  onMouseLeave={(e) => {
    e.currentTarget.style.backgroundColor = "transparent";
  }}
>
  Link
</Link>

// ✅ CORRECT - CSS hover with Tailwind
<Link className="hover:bg-card transition-colors duration-200">
  Link
</Link>
```

### ❌ Don't Use Inline Style Objects for Static Values

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - Inline style objects
<div
  style={{
    backgroundColor: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-page)",
    borderColor: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-200)",
    color: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-content)",
  }}
>

// ✅ CORRECT - Tailwind classes
<div className="bg-background text-foreground style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }}">
```

## ✅ Only 2 Valid Reasons for Custom CSS

### 1. Theme-Based Logo/Icon Switching

**✅ This is acceptable** - Tailwind can't handle theme-specific display logic:

```css
/* ✅ CORRECT - Theme-based visibility (can't be done with Tailwind) */
.nextjs-logo-light {
  display: block;
}
.nextjs-logo-dark {
  display: none;
}

[data-theme="modus-classic-dark"] .nextjs-logo-light,
[data-theme="modus-modern-dark"] .nextjs-logo-light {
  display: none;
}

[data-theme="modus-classic-dark"] .nextjs-logo-dark,
[data-theme="modus-modern-dark"] .nextjs-logo-dark {
  display: block;
}
```

### 2. Complex Animations

**✅ This is acceptable** - Requires `@keyframes` which Tailwind doesn't support:

```css
/* ✅ CORRECT - Complex @keyframes animation */
@keyframes slideInFromRight {
  0% {
    transform: translateX(100%);
    opacity: 0;
  }
  100% {
    transform: translateX(0);
    opacity: 1;
  }
}

.slide-in {
  animation: slideInFromRight 0.3s ease-out;
}
```

### ❌ Everything Else Uses Tailwind

**❌ DO NOT create custom classes for:**

- Colors (use `bg-*`, `text-*`, `border-*`)
- Spacing (use `p-*`, `m-*`, `gap-*`)
- Layout (use `flex`, `grid`, `items-*`)
- Hover states (use `hover:bg-*`)
- Focus states (use `focus:ring-*`)
- Borders (use `border`, `rounded-*`)
- Typography (use `text-*`, `font-*`)
- Responsive design (use `md:*`, `lg:*`)

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - Custom CSS class
.color-swatch {
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Tailwind inline
<div className="rounded-lg border style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }}">
```

## 📋 Migration Checklist

When refactoring from custom CSS to Tailwind:

- [ ] ✅ **Replace `.app-header`** → `bg-background text-foreground` + `style={{ borderBottom: "1px solid var(--border)" }}`
- [ ] ✅ **Replace `.app-footer`** → `bg-card text-foreground` + `style={{ borderTop: "2px solid var(--border)" }}`
- [ ] ✅ **Replace `.nav-link:hover`** → `hover:bg-card`
- [ ] ✅ **Replace `.text-foreground`** → `text-foreground`
- [ ] ✅ **Remove `onMouseEnter/Leave`** → Use `hover:` classes
- [ ] ✅ **Replace inline style objects** → Tailwind classes
- [ ] ✅ **Fix border violations** → Replace `border border-border` with `style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }}`
- [ ] ✅ **Test all interactive states** (hover, focus, active)
- [ ] ✅ **Verify theme switching** (light/dark themes)
- [ ] ✅ **Check responsive design** (mobile, tablet, desktop)

## 🎯 Benefits Summary

### Using Tailwind Inline:

1. **✅ No CSS Bloat**: Tailwind purges unused classes
2. **✅ Self-Documenting**: All styling visible in component
3. **✅ Better DX**: No file jumping to understand styles
4. **✅ Scalable**: Won't grow unmanageably
5. **✅ Maintainable**: Easy to modify inline
6. **✅ Performance**: No runtime style calculations
7. **✅ Type Safety**: Autocomplete for class names
8. **✅ Consistency**: Standard Tailwind patterns

### Minimizing Custom CSS:

1. **✅ Smaller Bundle**: Less CSS to parse and download
2. **✅ Easier Maintenance**: Fewer files to manage
3. **✅ Better Collaboration**: Standard Tailwind patterns everyone knows
4. **✅ Faster Development**: No need to name CSS classes
5. **✅ Less Conflicts**: No CSS specificity issues

## 🎯 Key Takeaways

1. **Use Tailwind inline** for 99% of styling
2. **NEVER create custom CSS classes** for colors, spacing, layout, hover states, etc.
3. **ONLY 2 exceptions**: Theme switching and complex `@keyframes` animations
4. **Use `hover:`, `focus:`, `active:`** prefixes instead of JavaScript or custom CSS
5. **Use design system colors** (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, etc.)
6. **Borders require width**: Use `style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }}`
7. **NEVER use `border border-border`** - This is a common violation!
8. **Keep `globals.css` minimal** - aim for <50 lines
9. **Test responsively** with Tailwind's `md:`, `lg:` prefixes
10. **Verify theme compatibility** - ensure light/dark themes work

